  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **The Recognition Scene** (1 review): Reviewer says it had not been played in a while before this show [6]\n- **Sacrifice (Palmcorder Yajna)** (1 review): Reviewer had never heard this song before; it turned out to be a big surprise [6]\n- **Riches and Wonders** (1 review): Reviewer found it exciting to hear this song performed live [5]\n- **No Children** (1 review): Reviewer was excited that this song was first played live at this show [6]\n- **My Favorite Things** (1 review): Played as one of the older favorites the reviewer says John pulled out during the set [4]\n- **Grendel's Mother** (1 review): Also named as an older favorite revived, alongside newer songs that were played well at the time [4]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **You're In Maya**: rare: 9 archived performances [8]\n- **Going To Queens**: rare: 14 archived performances [8]\n- **Sacrifice (Palmcorder Yajna)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [8]\n- **Riches and Wonders**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 7 archived performances [8]\n- **My Favorite Things**: rare: 13 archived performances [8]\n- **Going To Scotland**: rare: 12 archived performances [8]\n- **Ontario**: rare: 9 archived performances [8]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: The Mess Inside, No Children, See America Right [8]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg2002-10-23.aud.206mp3** (recommended): audience recording; 22 songs; 91 min [1]\n- **tmg2002-10-23**: source not stated; 22 songs; 91 min; rated 4.5/5 by 4 [2]. Said about its sound: The recording sounds pretty good, according to the reviewer [5]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer ranks it among the best Mountain Goats shows in the archive [4]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tmg2002-10-23.aud.206mp3**: Listed as an audience recording; the reviewer suspects it duplicates the other tmg2002-10-23 upload [7]\n- **tmg2002-10-23**: taped by Chris Bellew; transferred by Chris Bellew; source: SP-CMC-2>SP-SPSB-1>Sony PCM-M1@44.1Hz [2]",
